<h1 class=3D"headline">The lighthouse keepers of Kestrel Rock</h1>
<p class=3D"byline">By <a href=3D"https://coastal-gazette.example/authors/p=
riya-sharma" rel=3D"author">Priya Sharma</a> =C2=B7 <time datetime=3D"2026-=
11-20T07:30:00Z">20 November 2026</time></p>
<div class=3D"share-bar"><a href=3D"https://social.example/share">Share on =
Social</a> <a href=3D"mailto:?subject=3Dx">Share on Email</a></div>
<figure class=3D"lead-image"><img src=3D"https://coastal-gazette.example/me=
dia/keepers.jpg" alt=3D"The lighthouse on Kestrel Rock at dusk" width=3D"80=
0" height=3D"500"><figcaption>The lighthouse on Kestrel Rock, kept by hand =
until 1961.</figcaption></figure>
<div class=3D"story-body">
<p>For two hundred years the lighthouse on Kestrel Rock was kept by familie=
s who rowed out with the spring tide and stayed until the autumn gales. The=
 keepers wrote the weather into a ledger three times a day, and the ledgers=
 survive in a cupboard of the harbour office.</p>
<p>Mara Ellison, whose grandfather kept the light until 1961, has spent the=
 last year reading them page by page. She found storms that are still talke=
d about in the village, and quiet weeks in which the only entry is the colo=
ur of the sea.</p>
<div class=3D"ad-slot ad-inline">ADVERTISEMENT <a href=3D"https://ads.examp=
le/click2">Insure your cottage</a></div>
<h2>A life on the rock</h2>
<p>A life on the rock was ruled by the lamp and the clock. The wick was tri=
mmed at dusk and at midnight, the lens was polished every morning, and the =
brass was cleaned on Saturdays whatever the weather.</p>
<p>Supplies came by boat once a fortnight, and when the boat could not land=
 the keepers lived on salted fish and the potatoes they grew in a sheltered=
 corner of the rock.</p>
<blockquote><p>We were never lonely, Ellison remembers her grandfather sayi=
ng, because the sea was always talking.</p></blockquote>
<picture><source type=3D"image/webp" srcset=3D"https://coastal-gazette.exam=
ple/media/lamp.webp"><img src=3D"https://coastal-gazette.example/media/lamp=
.jpg" alt=3D"The old lamp" width=3D"640" height=3D"400"></picture>
<ul><li>Trim the wick at dusk and at midnight.</li><li>Polish the lens ever=
y morning.</li><li>Clean the brass on Saturdays.</li></ul>
<form class=3D"newsletter" action=3D"https://coastal-gazette.example/subscr=
ibe"><p>Subscribe to our newsletter for the week's best stories.</p><input =
type=3D"email" placeholder=3D"Your e-mail"><button>Subscribe</button></form=
>
<h2>The last keepers</h2>
<p>The light was automated in 1961, and the last keepers rowed ashore for g=
ood on a calm morning in October. The ledgers record it in a single line.<s=
up><a href=3D"https://coastal-gazette.example/2026/11/20/lighthouse-keepers=
#fn1" id=3D"r1">1</a></sup></p>
<table><thead><tr><th>Year</th><th>Keeper</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1=
893</td><td>Thomas Ellison</td></tr><tr><td>1961</td><td>John Ellison</td><=
/tr></tbody></table>
<p><img loading=3D"lazy" src=3D"data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAAAAA=
P///yH5BAEAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAIBRAA7" data-src=3D"https://coastal-gazette.ex=
ample/media/ledger.jpg" alt=3D"A page of the ledger"></p>
<p>The harbour office plans to put the ledgers on show next spring, beside =
the lamp that was taken down when the light went electric. Visitors will be=
 able to read the entries for the night of the great storm of 1893, when th=
e keepers kept the light burning for thirty hours without sleep.</p>
